    ],
    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "The Oxford/Hoyer Elevate is an electrically-operated, battery-powered Class III non-automatic weighing instrument (patient lift) manufactured by Joerns Healthcare, with a maximum capacity of 200 kg. The load cell is mounted between the internal faces of the mast; the two-piece plastic housing contains the electronics manufactured by IMS Inc. The hand control unit is used to lower and raise the boom and operate the legs. Devices: combined semi-automatic zero-setting and tare balancing devices, stable equilibrium indicator (HOLD), and digital averaging mode to allow weighing of unstable weights."
